ok   a cron task runs at its minute and not before
ok   tz: evaluates the expression in that zone; the default is config.scheduler_tz
ok   cron refuses a bad expression, an unknown zone, an empty or taken name
ok   the timetable survives a restart and a leader change
ok   a process that takes the lease over schedules from the table, not from its own guess
ok   a process that takes the lease over runs a cron slot the table records as due, once
ok   one process that misses the lease at a cron slot runs the slot at its next tick
ok   a missed cron slot is skipped unless catch_up
ok   a job: task enqueues and does not run the job on the scheduler thread
ok   a job: task needs a registered kind, and a block or job: but not both
ok   task_summary names cron tasks with their next run in UTC
ok   a cron task with no next run runs its due slot once, is reported once, then is skipped
ok   the timetable: rows read back as [last, next], 0 for a run that never happened
ok   the timetable never moves a row back; a new task's row never replaces one
ok   a cron task without tz: takes config.scheduler_tz as it is when the scheduler starts
ok   prune_schedules deletes the rows of names no longer registered
ok   config: scheduler_tz is UTC, from CYBERTRAIN_SCHEDULER_TZ, and boot refuses an unknown zone
ok   start! prunes the rows of names no longer registered
18 tests, 130 assertions, 0 failures
